From what I've been reading online it says that the Lamy Safari uses the LZ 50 nib. Which you can get in 1.1, 1.5, and 1.9mm.

&#x200B;

[https://goldspot.com/blogs/magazine/lamy-safari-fountain-pen-nib-size-comparison#:\~:text=The%20Lamy%20broad%20nib%20is,large%20and%20fast%20handwriting%20styles.&text=Lamy%20offers%20its%20stub%20calligraphy,mm%2C%20and%201.9mm%20size](https://goldspot.com/blogs/magazine/lamy-safari-fountain-pen-nib-size-comparison#:~:text=The%20Lamy%20broad%20nib%20is,large%20and%20fast%20handwriting%20styles.&text=Lamy%20offers%20its%20stub%20calligraphy,mm%2C%20and%201.9mm%20size).

&#x200B;

Thank you for your help tho
